.TH SMD 1 smd\-VERSION
.SH NAME
smd \- a small markdown (and barely\-html) viewer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smd
.RB [ \-v ]
.I file
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B smd
renders a markdown file (or, in a pinch, a simple html file) straight to
the screen using GTK, cairo and pango. No webkit, no javascript engine,
no network stack. Headings, bold/italic, inline and fenced code, links,
blockquotes, ordered/unordered lists, horizontal rules, images and LaTeX
math (inline
.B $..$
and block
.B $$..$$ )
are all supported.

Math is rasterized through
.BR pdflatex (1)
and
.BR pdftoppm (1)
if they're installed, and cached under
.IR ~/.cache/smd .
If they're missing, smd just shows the raw source instead of failing.

The file is watched with inotify and re-rendered automatically the
moment it changes on disk \- point your editor at it and treat the
window as a live preview.

.I file
is picked as markdown or html purely by its extension
.RI ( .md / .markdown
vs
.IR .html / .htm ).
The html path is deliberately minimal: no CSS, no layout engine, just
enough tag recognition to eyeball a document while you're writing it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-v
print version information and exit.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B j / k / Up / Down
scroll a line at a time.
.TP
.B space / Page Down
.TQ
.B shift+space / Page Up
scroll a page.
.TP
.B g / shift+g
jump to top / bottom.
.TP
.B + / \-
zoom in / out.
.TP
.B 0
reset zoom.
.TP
.B r
force a reload.
.TP
.B q
quit.
.PP
Clicking a link opens it with
.BR xdg-open (1) .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.cache/smd/
rendered LaTeX formulas, cached by content hash so re-rendering the
same document doesn't keep re-invoking latex.
.TP
.I config.h
compile-time configuration: colors, fonts, margins, keybindings. Copy
.I config.def.h
to
.I config.h
and edit before building to customize.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pdflatex (1),
.BR pdftoppm (1),
.BR xdg-open (1)
.SH BUGS
Nested emphasis (e.g. bold containing italic) isn't supported \- the
inline parser is intentionally flat. Lists are single-level. The html
mode has no idea what CSS is. Patches welcome, as always.
